content:
The sales tax rate of the owner's tax-and-title payment under the Physical Damage Coverage (Comprehensive and Collision) is the rate of the garaging state recorded on the Owner Auto Policy term the coverage belongs to.

| Garaging state of the Owner Auto Policy term | Sales tax rate (percent) |
|---|---|
| Texas | 6.25 |
| Georgia | 7.0 |
| Arizona | 5.6 |
| Ohio | 5.75 |
| Virginia | 4.15 |
| Any other state (Florida) | 6.0 (the home-state rate) |

**Hypothetical illustration.** On a tax base of 10,000.00 USD the sales tax comes to:
- 625.00 USD for an owner term garaged in Texas;
- 700.00 USD in Georgia;
- 560.00 USD in Arizona;
- 575.00 USD in Ohio;
- 415.00 USD in Virginia;
- 600.00 USD in Florida.
